                                                "sense_id": "d119f2bf-bb65-3009-a2ae-966cf06e27dd",
                                                "text": "From the fourteenth century onward, the successively smaller administrative subdivisions (pictagia, neighborhoods, contained vicinia) of cities like Lecce and Nardò were uniformly hagiotoponyms named after neighborhood churches."
